{"causes": ["The intense political and military upheavals of the late Roman Republic created a pressing need for contemporary historical documentation.", "His aristocratic background and direct involvement in major military campaigns, such as the Sertorian War, provided him with unique insights and firsthand material.", "The established tradition of Roman annalists and historians like Fabius Pictor and Cato the Elder inspired the pursuit of historiography as a noble civic duty."], "effects": ["His "Historiae" provided a crucial, albeit fragmentary, contemporary account of the Sullan era and the Sertorian War, influencing later Roman historiography.", "His work served as a primary source for subsequent historians like Sallust, who drew upon Sisenna's narratives to inform their own historical compositions.", "He contributed to the evolving tradition of Roman historiography, blending annalistic style with more detailed narrative and personal experience."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "lucius-cornelius-sisenna", "sourceName": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "sertorian-war", "targetName": "Sertorian War", "context": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna served as a legatus under Pompey during the Sertorian War from 76 to 72 BCE."}, {"sourceSlug": "lucius-cornelius-sisenna", "sourceName": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "historiae-by-sisenna", "targetName": "Historiae (by Sisenna)", "context": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna authored the "Historiae," a multi-volume historical work covering Roman events from 90 BCE to 67 BCE."}, {"sourceSlug": "sulla", "sourceName": "Sulla", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "lucius-cornelius-sisenna", "targetName": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna", "context": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna's military and political career, including his praetorship, occurred during and was shaped by the dominance of Sulla."}, {"sourceSlug": "lucius-cornelius-sisenna", "sourceName": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "roman-republic", "targetName": "Roman Republic", "context": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna's life and career as a soldier and historian were entirely situated within the late Roman Republic."}, {"sourceSlug": "pompey-the-great", "sourceName": "Pompey the Great", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "lucius-cornelius-sisenna", "targetName": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna", "context": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna served as a legatus under Pompey during campaigns against Sertorius and the pirates."}], "places": [{"name": "Rome, Roman Republic", "role": "Political Center"}, {"name": "Hispania, Roman Republic", "role": "Military Service"}, {"name": "Crete, Roman Republic", "role": "Place of Death"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Lucius Cornelius Sisenna", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "lucius-cornelius-sisenna"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q709628", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Cornelius_Sisenna"], "tags": ["Journalists & Chroniclers", "cause-and-effect", "cultural-diffusion", "temporal-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna's contemporary "Historiae," despite being largely lost, provided a crucial eyewitness account of the Sullan era and Sertorian War, influencing major later historians like Sallust. His work contributed significantly to the development of Roman historiography during a period of immense political upheaval.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-06-08T13:50:18Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#27141546625", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna was a Roman soldier, historian, and annalist. He was praetor in 78 BC.", "newValue": "Lucius Cornelius Sisenna, a prominent Roman soldier, politician, and historian, served as praetor in 78 BCE and distinguished himself during the tumultuous late Roman Republic. His primary significance lies in his extensive historical work, the "Historiae," which chronicled Roman affairs from the Social War (90 BCE) to the end of the Sertorian War (67 BCE). This period, marked by civil strife, the rise of Sulla, and the emergence of figures like Pompey, was pivotal, and Sisenna's account offered a contemporary perspective from an active participant.

Sisenna's military career saw him serve as a legatus under Sulla, likely participating in the campaigns against Mithridates and later in the Sullan civil wars. He then held the praetorship, a crucial step in the *cursus honorum*. His most notable military service came during the Sertorian War (76-72 BCE) in Hispania, where he served under Pompey the Great. During this conflict, Sisenna was tasked with military operations, and it was in the course of these duties, or shortly after, that he compiled his detailed observations into his magnum opus. He died in 66 BCE on Crete while serving under Pompey during the campaign against the pirates, a testament to his lifelong commitment to Roman service.

Despite the unfortunate loss of almost all of his "Historiae"—only fragments and citations by later authors like Sallust, Livy, and Velleius Paterculus survive—Sisenna's work was highly regarded in antiquity. Sallust, in particular, drew upon Sisenna's accounts for his own history of the Jugurthine War and Catilinarian Conspiracy, suggesting Sisenna's narrative prowess and factual accuracy. His work served as a vital bridge between earlier annalistic traditions and the more sophisticated historical narratives that emerged in the late Republic, providing an eyewitness perspective on events that shaped the transition from Republic to Empire."}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-08T13:50:18Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#27141546625", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Classical era: flourishing of philosophical inquiry, imperial expansion, and codification of la", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "118 BCE, Ancient Rome"}, {"title": "Rise of print media and public discourse", "type": "Idea", "year": "118 BCE, Ancient Rome"}], "newValue": ["The intense political and military upheavals of the late Roman Republic created a pressing need for contemporary historical documentation.", "His aristocratic background and direct involvement in major military campaigns, such as the Sertorian War, provided him with unique insights and firsthand material.", "The established tradition of Roman annalists and historians like Fabius Pictor and Cato the Elder inspired the pursuit of historiography as a noble civic duty."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-08T13:50:18Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#27141546625", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Shaped public opinion and historical record", "type": "Idea", "year": "66 BCE"}, {"title": "Contributed to enduring intellectual and institutional frameworks shaping subsequent civilizati", "type": "Movement", "year": "66 BCE"}], "newValue": ["His "Historiae" provided a crucial, albeit fragmentary, contempo